d5=A.a(["The p-value measures the compatibility of the data with the null hypothesis AND all model assumptions: it is the probability of observing data at least as extreme if these assumptions were true.",'It is not the probability that the null hypothesis is true, nor the probability that the result is "due to chance", nor a measure of clinical importance.',"p > 0.05 does not prove the absence of an effect: look at the CI. If the CI contains both 0 and clinically important effects, the study simply did not reach a conclusion.","Concluding that there is no relevant difference requires a margin set a priori and a CI lying entirely within that margin (equivalence logic)."],c5)
