h9=A.a(["A confounder is related to the exposure and to the outcome without lying on the causal path. It can create, hide or reverse an association.","Simpson's paradox is its extreme form: the direction of the crude association reverses in every stratum.","Adjustment corrects only factors that are measured, well measured and correctly modelled: residual confounding remains possible. Only randomization also balances unknown factors.",'Wording: "was associated with", not "causes", in an observational study.',"Propensity score: the probability of being treated given the measured confounders. Matching or weighting on this score makes the groups comparable on these factors; this is checked with standardized differences (< 0.1), never with tests. The score does not correct unmeasured confounding."],c5)
