j4=A.a(["When the outcome is a time (to death, to relapse) and some subjects are lost to follow-up or still event-free at the end of follow-up, their time is CENSORED: we only know it exceeds the last known date.","Analysing the event as a binary variable without a common horizon of complete follow-up, or excluding censored subjects, biases the results.","The Cox model estimates ratios of instantaneous rates (hazard ratios, HR) without assuming the form of the baseline hazard, provided this ratio is constant over time (proportional hazards) and censoring is not informative.","An HR is neither a cumulative risk ratio nor a survival difference at a date: to communicate impact, add survival curves or proportions at a given horizon.","The proportionality test (cox.zph) has little power with few events: a non-significant result does not prove proportionality."],c5)
